.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt NVMFADM 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nvmfadm
.Nd administer NVMe over Fabrics target subsystems
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Cm create-subsys
.Op Fl p Ar portid
.Op Fl s Ar serial
.Ar subnqn
.Nm
.Cm delete-subsys
.Ar subnqn
.Nm
.Cm list-subsys
.Nm
.Cm restore
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility creates, deletes and lists the NVM subsystems of the
.Xr nvmft 4D
target port provider.
Each subsystem is one STMF target port, named by its subsystem NQN.
A logical unit that has a view on that target is a namespace of the
subsystem; the namespace ID is the view's logical unit number plus one.
Logical units, views, host groups and target groups are managed with
.Xr sbdadm 8
and
.Xr stmfadm 8 .
.Pp
Subsystems are saved in the STMF configuration, so the
.Sy svc:/system/stmf:default
service must be online.
The
.Sy svc:/system/nvmf/target:default
service creates the saved subsystems again each time it starts.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ar
.It Xo
.Cm create-subsys
.Op Fl p Ar portid
.Op Fl s Ar serial
.Ar subnqn
.Xc
Create the subsystem
.Ar subnqn
and save it.
The name must be a valid NQN, for example
.Sy nqn.2026-01.com.example:storage:disk0 .
The new target port comes online if STMF brings new target ports online,
which is its default.
.Bl -tag -width Ar
.It Fl p Ar portid
The port ID reported to hosts, from 0 to 65535.
The default is 1.
.It Fl s Ar serial
The serial number reported by the subsystem's controllers, up to 20
characters.
The default is derived from the system's host ID.
.El
.It Cm delete-subsys Ar subnqn
Delete the subsystem
.Ar subnqn
and remove it from the saved configuration.
The command fails while any host is connected to the subsystem.
.It Cm list-subsys
Print the NQN of each subsystem, one to a line.
.It Cm restore
Create each saved subsystem that does not already exist.
The target service runs this command when it starts.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Sy Example 1
Exporting a ZFS volume as namespace 1 of a new subsystem
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# zfs create -V 10G tank/vol0
# stmfadm create-lu /dev/zvol/rdsk/tank/vol0
Logical unit created: 600144F0C73A8B0000005F1D3F5B0001
# nvmfadm create-subsys nqn.2026-01.com.example:storage:vol0
# stmfadm create-tg vol0-tg
# stmfadm offline-target nqn.2026-01.com.example:storage:vol0
# stmfadm add-tg-member -g vol0-tg \e
    nqn.2026-01.com.example:storage:vol0
# stmfadm online-target nqn.2026-01.com.example:storage:vol0
# stmfadm add-view -t vol0-tg -n 0 600144F0C73A8B0000005F1D3F5B0001
# svcadm enable svc:/system/nvmf/target:default
.Ed
.Sh INTERFACE STABILITY
The command line interface of
.Nm
is
.Sy Uncommitted .
The output of
.Nm
is
.Sy Not-An-Interface
and may change at any time.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nvmft 4D ,
.Xr nvmfd 8 ,
.Xr sbdadm 8 ,
.Xr stmfadm 8
